Z||000000||ChadMan||09-06-2001||09:39 PM||||Sorry it took me so long, but I finally drove by 704 Middlebury Way in Powell for you.  It's a private residence in an upper-middle-class neighborhood...there is no JD Wheels signage or anything to indicate it's a business of any kind.<P>Anybody wondering what the heck this is about can get the scoop here:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/009739.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/009739.html</A> <P>||||reg||3
Z||000001||Joe Torma||09-07-2001||03:54 AM||||Wow...thanks for the driving by.  I appreciate it!  If you need anyone in 'Jersey checked out I'll return the favor.<P>I guess I should have posted an update, but we just resolved things this past Friday.  JDwheels.com went on vacation apparently--and didn't tell anyone.  They charged the card, because they showed 4 rims in stock at their "warehouse"...but really, the warehouse had 3 wheels only.  So they shipped nothing.<P>Anyway we got a good deal on our new selection.<P>Thanks again...interesting it isn't a shop or anything!!!<P>Joe<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig.gif">  <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A> ||||reg||1
